"The Emperor knows what the Fateweavers are, and an early injunction keeps the throne free of Fate."
"The throne is one check on the Fateweavers and the Demiurge another; both exist by their leave."
"Most Fateweavers support keeping the throne as a check on their own number."
"The Emperor called arcanists to service reluctantly, persuaded by Demiurge Caldwell, not the Weavers."
"The Spires the Army now guards each imprison a chained augera; soldiers and public do not know it."
"The augera web guards every citizen from outsiders and reports attacks for the Fateweavers to meet."
"The agents guard Academy freshmen from the attackers and also watch them with suspicion."
"Agents have orders to bring runaway students back to safehouses unharmed, never to kill them."
"SD-P1 is the Chosen One's detail, led by Ms Pearl; SD-P7 is Caden Dundale's, led by Mr Silver."
"Safehouse 3 is the Ka'atryn mansion in Geldor's High District."
"The agency's head is a woman in her sixties, bone-white hair in a bun, green eyes; agents say ma'am."
"Using a personal glyph an agent gives brings help but ties the user tighter into prophetic links."
"The Academy and the Empire do not always see eye to eye; agents consult the Demiurge reluctantly."
"Duke Ka'atryn's pull got Nightwatchers set on his son and his son's friends."
"Nightwatchers have guarded the Chosen One since the Prophecy was revealed to him."
"The Chosen One's Nightwatchers defer to him on some matters."
"Some Nightwatchers carry wysana, intelligent constructs of pure arcana, as few others may."
"Nightwatchers know overcharge sequences that burst an artefact's power at risk of wrecking it."
"Their ultimate defence tracks any arcanic attack to its source and destroys it, veiled or not."
"The ultimate defence uses glyphs from unknown sets, learned by rote; it drains a gestalt near hollow."
"Kant and Reeves at the Academy have ties to the Fateweavers."
"Bertram, the Academy smuggler, is the son of a police detective who may be on his trail."
